    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "recompile",
        "title": "Reassemble model artifacts with optional tensor overrides",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "util/recompile.py accepts input/output directories, an optional YAML override specification and an 8192 shard-size default. Neither directory option is argparse-required. main constructs Config and an unloaded default-component Model, installs overrides into config.stc, estimates decoder/head storage, then calls compile_model with model_stc=True and tokenizer=None. The separately constructed local stc and local size helpers are unused.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d24b382b157f43d893a51bcdb01ace68",
              "call_43d35fc26216465b856ac524df6bed13"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Overrides map sources[].id to sources[].model_dir and overrides[].key to the selected source. Keys are grouped by source directory, then passed as fnmatch filters to VariantSafetensorsCollection.add_stc. A later added collection wins overlapping matches; an unmatched key falls back to the original collection. A matched but missing replacement tensor does not fall back.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d24b382b157f43d893a51bcdb01ace68",
              "call_e2b82f9a5c4640a1a4af99ea7d850ef1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Whole-parent search found existing variant-construction callers in model_init.init and eval/model_diff.py. Both use the same YAML grouping and routing preparation. model_init installs overrides before constructing the model; model_diff, like recompile, constructs the model first. Those paths subsequently load tensors, whereas recompile passes the collection directly to artifact assembly. None of these inspected override blocks validates replacement shapes or completeness.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_36846b166f504ea0a91cbf8cbac6035c",
              "call_6fb53b3ef44648b3965839ae915aa1d4",
              "call_d56f097656064a2cb3eda72271d2ba38",
              "call_d24b382b157f43d893a51bcdb01ace68"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Model.get_storage_info retains its three-value return and lm_head suffix classification. Loaded modules still count tensor payload bits; unloaded modules now sum header payload bytes under module.key and multiply by eight. Decoder BPW divides counted non-head Linear bits by their padded weight counts; head BPW is separate. vram_bits includes those selected linears, not all model tensors or runtime allocations.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_01a94020c0054da5bbe1e5cfafb0e042",
              "call_876b2d0527304b2e9c054e294df69cf9",
              "call_68c10a5d0f3440378fa44484eaae7fd2",
              "call_e2b82f9a5c4640a1a4af99ea7d850ef1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "This accounting change supplies a precondition for the new unloaded workflow: Module starts with device=None and Linear.get_tensors returns an empty dictionary when unloaded. Existing direct Model-method callers in eval/longctx.py, eval/ppl.py and examples/batched_translation.py all first load through model_init.init and retain the same tuple unpacking. The separate comparison-adapter helpers found by search are not calls to this Model method.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_1903221e14d64437b85646226cfa6961",
              "call_68c10a5d0f3440378fa44484eaae7fd2",
              "call_f0b3897b3fe2481e9c5f337030a9fec1",
              "call_cd32723caa0b4a9a9d7471ef1767f84f",
              "call_4b31a6f4ffe14bdf9810e9f319124842",
              "call_d006c6165fc74a6b82fbbd93e0158962",
              "call_6fb53b3ef44648b3965839ae915aa1d4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "compile_model selects config.stc only when args.get('model_stc') is truthy; otherwise its original work_dir/qtensors source remains. The sole existing direct caller found in conversion/convert_model.py still supplies prepared conversion arguments and follows that original branch. The new utility bypasses conversion's calibration and per-module quantization work, not merely its command-line parser.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_dc944adf87cd421b8c54da53bfad2b81",
              "call_4427c98a82f143c7a6d9748be8b2b1f5",
              "call_dac51fe42a134e58908b6ec290c503fa",
              "call_6c23f0fd43f1447b96bdc06540601b97",
              "call_d24b382b157f43d893a51bcdb01ace68"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Assembly still packs whole top-level modules, preserves BF16 on reads, makes tensors contiguous and writes safetensors shards. shard_size is multiplied by 1024\u00b2, so the default is 8 GiB despite the MB help text. Oversized modules receive a warning rather than being split. Auxiliary files are copied from the original input directory; replacement directories contribute selected tensors, not their configuration or tokenizer files.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_528e4f822ae14d2da83a69ce7c7446e5",
              "call_d24b382b157f43d893a51bcdb01ace68"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Existing quantization_config is retained with only bits and head_bits overwritten. The utility rounds measured decoder storage BPW to two decimals and head storage BPW to an integer. When the input lacks quantization_config, the original metadata-construction branch still requires calibration and output-scale arguments. create_quantization_config_json subsequently reopens the output and derives per-leaf tensor_storage metadata from its stored tensor headers.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_dc944adf87cd421b8c54da53bfad2b81",
              "call_d24b382b157f43d893a51bcdb01ace68",
              "call_f09daf3e1ede4122af38da04f9b7740b",
              "call_7d2e1dadccb24fb68131b9d3c6cfc5fb"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A bounded scalar transcription confirmed the default shard target is 8589934592 bytes. It also demonstrated that original-name enumeration omits a replacement-only .mcg tensor: an illustrative 2048-weight group reports 4.0 BPW instead of 4.015625. Transcribing the utility's arguments through the metadata fallback raises KeyError('cal_rows'). These checks do not execute repository code or load tensors.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_48c5408733c541cc860ef90b43c97028"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The linear.py edit only adds \u201cTODO: Why copy here?\u201d to the existing FP32 capture conversion. It neither removes copy=True nor changes Hessian accumulation.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_bf01d23f4c834e6db527ce2fcae1298f",
              "call_68c10a5d0f3440378fa44484eaae7fd2"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
